  "description": "When I don't feel like cranking up the oven, I turn to this technique, which delivers a squash soup that's made 100% on the stovetop, in just about half an hour.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: 3 sprigs fresh thyme (optional); 1/2 cup heavy cream (optional); 1 to 2 tablespoons brown or white sugar (optional, see notes)\n\nOptional substitutions: homemade chicken stock → vegetable stock\n\nNotes: You can also use maple syrup or honey in place of the sugar if desired.\nGlazed pecans make a great garnish when serving (or try this recipe, but swap pecans for the almonds). You can also sprinkle with minced fresh herbs like chives, parsley, or sage. Try drizzling with browned butter or olive oil if desired.",
